## Fix Graph sidebar stuck on Mapping Studio (?section=design&tab=build)

Context: After Mapping was hosted under Graph, clicking any Graph sidebar
item appeared to stay on Studio with URL ``/dtwin/?section=design&tab=build``.
Root cause: ``mapping-init-section.js`` injects a pre-paint ``display: … !important``
style that was never cleared on Graph, locking the first URL section; and
``SidebarNav._pushSectionState`` preserved Build's ``?tab=build`` when leaving
``sync``, producing sticky ``design&tab=build`` URLs.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/js/sidebar-nav.js
   Clear ``#initial-section-style`` on every section activation; drop foreign
   ``?tab=`` params when navigating away from the section that owns them.
2. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-init.js
   Hosted-on-Graph bootstrap also clears the pre-paint style after SidebarNav
   takes over (covers default Explorer landings).
3. tests/units/front/test_sidebar_nav_section_url.py
   Contracts for style clear + tab scrubbing.
4. tests/e2e/dtwin/test_dtwin_flows.py
   Sidebar parity includes Mapping sections (information/design/manual) + sync.

