## Pattern detection: forward-only walks

Context:
Pattern detection walked every triple both ways: each relation produced an `out`
and an `in` edge row, and every hop followed both. That doubled the edge table,
put a `direction` field into every token and typed edge, drew reversed arrows in
the diagram, and let a walk step back along an inbound relation. The user asked
for forward-only walks (subject → object). Spec:
`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-16-pattern-forward-only-design.md`.

Changes:

1. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py
   `build_directed_edges` emits one row per eligible triple (no reversed copy,
   no `direction` column). `build_hop` walks `_dir` forward only; `expanded`,
   the structural and neighbour-attribute tokens, and `typed_edges` drop
   `direction`. `init_tokens` DDL and `write_shape_edges` drop it too. The
   preview-edge filter `direction = 'out'` is removed. Hub degree is now
   out-degree.
2. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/pattern_diagram.py
   Edges no longer carry `direction`. `_attribute_of` parses the two token
   shapes (anchor `0||type|self|prop|bin`, neighbour `hop|via|type|prop|bin`).
3. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/JobPatterns.py
   `shape_edges_query` no longer selects `direction`.
4. src/front/static/intelligence/js/intelligence-patterns.js
   Arrows always point at the child (`marker-end`); the `patArrowIn` marker is
   removed.
5. src/front/templates/partials/intelligence/_intel_patterns_saved.html
   Help text describes forward walks and the token layout without direction.
6. tests/units/core/test_pattern_job_sql.py
   Fixtures and expectations updated for forward walks. The hub fixture uses a
   node with many outgoing relations. The shell test now covers a cycle. New
   `TestForwardOnlyWalk` covers inbound-only anchors and dead ends.
7. tests/units/core/test_pattern_diagram.py
   Tokens and edges without direction; attribute chips checked for both shapes.
8. tests/units/core/test_saved_pattern_store.py
   Fixture `shape_edges` table without `direction`.
9. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-16-pattern-forward-only-design.md (new)
   Design, behaviour changes, deployment notes.
10. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-pattern-detection-design.md
    Algorithm step 2 points to the amendment; the `direction` field is removed
    from the hop record.
11. docs/user-guide.md and docs/architecture.md
    Pattern walk description: forward only, inbound relations not walked, hub
    pruning on out-degree.

Behaviour changes:
- Every `pattern_id` changes once (tokens no longer carry the direction).
- Anchors that are only the object of relations get empty neighbourhoods.
- Saved patterns keep the snapshot they were saved from until re-saved.

