## Diagram chains keep the predicate that reached the parent

Context:
The Patterns diagram drew `Customer -hasContract-> Contract -hasContract->
Customer` for the Addison Martin pattern, though no such path exists. The
diagram node was `(hop, type)`, so all hop-1 Contracts merged into one node,
and hop-2 typed edges were aggregated by `(parent_type, via, child_type)`. Chains
therefore spliced edges from different Contracts. The walk direction was not
the cause. Decision: node identity includes the incoming predicate. Pattern
signatures (`pattern_id`) are unchanged.

Changes:

1. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py (`PatternSQL`)
   - `build_frontier_0`: frontier rows carry `via` (`''` for the anchor).
   - `build_hop`: frontier is `(anchor, node, via)`; `expanded` carries
     `parent_via`; tokens are emitted from `SELECT DISTINCT anchor, parent,
     node, via, node_type`, so the token multiset is unchanged; typed edges
     group by `parent_via`.
   - `init_tokens`: `typed_edges` gains `parent_via`.
   - `write_shape_edges`: `<out>_shape_edges` gains `parent_via`.
2. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/pattern_diagram.py
   Node id is `hop|via|type` (the token prefix); `_attribute_of` and the edge
   builder use it; each edge starts from the parent's `(hop-1, parent_via, type)`
   node. Node dict gains `via` / `via_label`.
3. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/JobPatterns.py
   `shape_edges_query` selects `parent_via`.
4. tests/units/core/test_pattern_job_sql.py
   `TestForwardOnlyWalk.test_chain_hangs_off_the_predicate_that_reached_it`
   (Addison shape: hop-2 edge is under the hasPolicy Contract only).
5. tests/units/core/test_pattern_diagram.py
   Rows carry `parent_via`; node ids are `hop|via|type`; new
   `test_same_type_reached_by_two_predicates_keeps_its_own_chain`.
6. tests/units/core/test_saved_pattern_store.py
   Fixture `shape_edges` table gains `parent_via`.
7. docs/architecture.md, docs/user-guide.md,
   docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-16-pattern-forward-only-design.md
   Describe the new node identity and the known limit.

Known limit: the parent is remembered one level only. Chains of three or more
hops can still splice two hop-1 branches that share a predicate and type at
hop 2. Full-path keys would remove it at the cost of more shape-edge rows.

Deployment / data:
Detect output tables are rebuilt on the next Detect. Saved snapshots keep their
stored `diagram_json` (old `hop|type` ids) until the pattern is saved again.
Performance: a node reached through k predicates now has k frontier rows; the
Databricks job cost grows with that multiplicity. To be measured on a real
domain.

