=== Pattern catalog save: constant statement count (was 2 warehouse queries per pattern) ===

Context: on the 100M-triple `bigcustomers100m` domain Detect's Spark job takes
about 5.5 min (stage_ms: prep 78s, hops 127s, signatures 45s), but the
background task then sat in "Saving pattern catalog" for 55+ minutes. `save()`
looped over every pattern of the run (46,754) and ran two sequential warehouse
queries per pattern (`_shapes` and `_shape_edges`, ~200 ms each) to build each
diagram. The earlier "catalog-only" save removed the member fan-out but kept
this per-pattern loop; it was never measured on a run this large.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/SavedPatternStore.py
   `save()` now issues a constant number of statements: it reads the focus
   plus the top `EAGER_DIAGRAMS` (100) patterns by support in bulk (shapes,
   KPIs, edges: 3 queries), writes those rows with their diagram, and writes
   every other pattern with ONE server-side `INSERT ... SELECT` over
   `<out>_shapes` joined to aggregated `<out>_shape_edges` (KPIs computed in
   the warehouse, `diagram_json` empty). `shape()` already rebuilds a missing
   diagram from live Detect on first open and persists it. `_payload_from_rows`
   extracted from `_live_shape_payload`; `_metrics_from` and
   `_detect_pattern_ids` removed (replaced by `_eager_pattern_ids`).
2. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/saved_pattern_sql.py (new)
   Pure SQL builders (`kpi_sql`, `insert_catalog_sql`, `insert_rest_sql`,
   `sql_lit`), extracted to keep `SavedPatternStore` under the 800-LOC budget.
3. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/JobPatterns.py
   `shapes_bulk_query`, `shape_edges_bulk_query` (per-pattern cap via
   `ROW_NUMBER`), `fetch_shape_edges_for` (grouped by pattern, same legacy
   `parent_via` fallback and missing-table contract as `fetch_shape_edges`;
   fallback logic shared in `_edge_rows_with_fallback`).
4. tests/units/core/test_saved_pattern_store.py, test_job_patterns.py
   Statement count independent of pattern count (400 extra patterns),
   SQL-computed KPIs equal the Python ones, lazy diagram beyond the eager cap
   is drawn and persisted on first open, missing edges table, bulk edge reader
   grouping / legacy fallback / missing table.
5. docs/user-guide.md, docs/architecture.md: save behaviour and new module.

Measured on the real warehouse (46,754 patterns, Detect output of
`graph_patterns_bigcustomers100m_2`): the `INSERT ... SELECT` for all patterns
takes 6 s; the three eager bulk reads take about 1.5 s each. Previous
behaviour: 55+ min and still running.

Behaviour note: patterns outside the focus + top-100 have no stored diagram
until first opened; if a new Detect replaces the live tables before that, such
a pattern shows its KPIs and shape tokens but no diagram.

